<title>USA: Senator--Honda to build plant in S.Carolina.</title>
<headline>Senator--Honda to build plant in S.Carolina.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honda Motor Co. will break ground Monday for a plant in South Carolina to build all-terrain vehicles, Democratic Senator Ernest Hollings said Thursday.</p>
<p>Hollings' office said the plant would cost $30 million to $40 million and will employ about 700 people.    The plant</p>
<p>will be located in Timmonsville near Florence, South Carolina, Hollings said.</p>
<p>He discussed the plant during a meeting of the Senate Commerce Committee.</p>
